/target/
/build/
# Codegen output and the lock that names it — both USER-side, like every other
# bench leaf. This file was the only one in nros-bench missing these two lines,
# which is how a `generated/` tree and its `Cargo.lock` came to be committed
# here and nowhere else.
/generated/
/Cargo.lock
# The owned entry is its own cargo root (phase-531 W7); its lock is seeded
# from the pin set on build, never committed.
/src/*/Cargo.lock
# The workspace's packages sit under `src/`, and codegen writes each one's
# message crates beside its `package.xml` (issue 2470).
/src/*/generated/
